A failed fdatasync that cannot publish its degraded state, for want of memory,
throws std::bad_alloc in its place and leaves the engine healthy, with writes
acknowledged that nothing confirmed durable. Reverts #618. The sweep of
create_manifest's failed fdatasync catches it too.
Guarded-by: "alloc sweep: set_mode(Follower) whose fdatasync fails"

